        "original_id": "c823dd63-2c65-5c16-bc00-6fd1ae3e4f47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: 247 Cherry, General Motors Building\n- Places: Lower East Side, Manhattan, New York City, 767 Fifth Avenue\n- Companies: SHoP Architects, JDS Development Group, Edward Durell Stone & Associates, Emery Roth & Sons\n- Topics: residential buildings, office towers, international style\n\nFacts:\n- In 1968, the General Motors Building was completed as a 50-story, 705-foot office tower at 767 Fifth Avenue in Manhattan, New York City.\n- The General Motors Building was designed in the international style by Edward Durell Stone & Associates with Emery Roth & Sons.\n- 247 Cherry is a seventy-seven-story residential building under development in the Lower East Side neighborhood of Manhattan, New York City.\n- 247 Cherry was designed by SHoP Architects and is being developed by JDS Development Group.",
